        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet on an impressive site of approximately 1.75 acres, this substantial unfinished residence offers a rare opportunity to complete and customise a superb family home to your own specification. Extending to approximately 313 sq. m. (3,369 sq. ft.), the property is currently weather tight and provides generously proportioned accommodation throughout.\n\nThe ground floor layout comprises a welcoming entrance hall, spacious living room, sitting room, large kitchen/dining area, conservatory, utility room, study, play room and two guest toilets. Upstairs, the first floor offers five well-appointed bedrooms, three of which benefit from ensuite bathrooms, together with a large family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the property enjoys a large site with excellent potential for landscaped gardens, outdoor entertaining areas or further enhancement, subject to the necessary permissions. A large detached garage is also located on site, providing excellent storage or workshop potential.\n\nThis is an ideal opportunity for purchasers seeking a spacious countryside home with the freedom to complete the interiors to their own taste and standard.\n\nLocation: \nProperty is loacted just 4.5km from Strokestown. \nStrokestown is a vibrant heritage town renowned for its rich history, welcoming community and scenic countryside setting. The town offers an excellent range of amenities including schools, shops, cafés, restaurants, sporting facilities and everyday services, while retaining its charming traditional character.\n\nConveniently positioned within easy reach of Roscommon Town, Longford and major road networks, Strokestown combines rural charm with accessibility, offering an excellent quality of life for families and commuters alike.\n\nNote: \nThese particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Whilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither DNG McGill nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars. No person in the employment of DNG McGill has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property."
